<p>Thailand&#x27;s parliament voted on Thursday to keep Anutin Charnvirakul in office as prime minister. Reports said he won 293 votes, clearing the majority threshold among the 498 lawmakers present in the House of Representatives. The result gives Thailand a confirmed leader as it faces fresh economic pressure linked to turmoil in the Middle East. SCMP reported that the U.S.-Israeli war on Iran was costing Thailand tens of millions of dollars a day in fuel-price support.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/SnwEGWunNSYkLFD2DFcUIBKkINCw2My2Bek9xvY-7OOlnXEP1AxI84ZtEcZRqPhv6TcaypZ5kwaWiwDUsctNQ49tbTNREQT-d5AVMJg9fvREX1d7kysIcnDmMjuVKsvo2BE1nVO1t61KvUJxBoejqzTCQteOa5XQBp28ESEZcA' alt='Thailand&#x27;s parliamentary vote confirms Anutin Charnvirakul as prime minister.' /><br /><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Anutin Charnvirakul: Before the vote, he told lawmakers he would reset Thailand after years of weak growth and political crisis. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/southeast-asia/article/3347127/pm-anutin-takes-charge-thailand-mideast-chaos-pressures-economy'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Analysts cited by DW: They see Anutin&#x27;s selection as a chance to restore political stability in Thailand. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/thailand-elects-anutin-charnvirakul-as-new-prime-minister/a-76425154'>Deutsche Welle</a>)</li><li>Thailand&#x27;s conservative establishment: SCMP described the parliamentary result as a political win for conservative forces after years of conflict with pro-democracy movements. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/southeast-asia/article/3347127/pm-anutin-takes-charge-thailand-mideast-chaos-pressures-economy'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/thailand-prime-minister-anutin-charnvirakul-to-remain-in-power-following-parliament-vote/article70760942.ece'>Thailand Prime Minister Anutin Charnvirakul to remain in power following Parliament vote</a> -